From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Juan Pablo Lassala <jpablolassala@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 04:42:20 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] main: Skip the windowmanager required component under Camino

On X11, mate-session starts Marco as its windowmanager required component.
Under Camino, the compositor is mate-session's parent and is already running,
so Marco must not start, and it could not: it needs to be the X window manager,
which Camino already is on XWayland.

Skip the component in append_required_apps when MATE_WM_NAME is Camino. The
WindowManager phase then has no app and ends at once. Without that variable,
nothing changes.
---
 mate-session/main.c | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/mate-session/main.c b/mate-session/main.c
index 4b3ddae..e655d43 100644
--- a/mate-session/main.c
+++ b/mate-session/main.c
@@ -267,6 +267,16 @@ static void append_required_apps(GsmManager* manager)
 
 			component = required_components[i];
 
+			/* Camino is the compositor, and it is already running: it started
+			 * mate-session. So there is no window manager to start, and the
+			 * WindowManager phase has no app to wait for. */
+			if (g_strcmp0(component, "windowmanager") == 0 &&
+			    g_strcmp0(g_getenv("MATE_WM_NAME"), "Camino") == 0)
+			{
+				g_debug("main: skipping component '%s' under Camino", component);
+				continue;
+			}
+
 			default_provider = g_settings_get_string (settings_required_components, component);
 
 			g_debug ("main: %s looking for component: '%s'", component, default_provider);
